course: dictionary
lesson: 5538
title: Legal means allowed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Legal means allowed by the law, or to do with the law and courts. Read the words around it to find the clues. «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems and report weaknesses; permission is what makes it legal.» The permission is the clue: legal means the rules say yes.
explain: Legal can also mean to do with lawyers and courts. «A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with legal things» means a solicitor helps with matters of the law. In a game, a legal move is one that the rules allow.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «There are legal ways to learn security: puzzle games, competitions and courses» can become «There are ways to learn security that are allowed», and it still makes sense. So legal means allowed.
fact: Legal means allowed by the law of a country or place.
fact: Legal also means to do with the law, courts and lawyers, as in legal advice or a legal case.
fact: In games and sports, a legal move is one that follows the rules.
fact: «Legal» is the opposite of illegal, which means not allowed by the law.
fact: Legal tender is money that must be accepted as payment.
exercise: «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems.» What makes their work legal? | Working at night | *Written permission | Being very fast | Wearing dark clothes
exercise: «A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with legal things.» What does legal mean here? | *To do with the law and courts | Very old | Very hungry | Brightly lit
exercise: A «legal move» in chess is one that does what? | Is slow and careful | Is made by the oldest player | Captures the most pieces | *Follows the rules of the game
test: Which word is the opposite of legal? | Lawful | *Illegal | Lawyer | Allowed
test: Legal tender means money that is what? | Only for children to spend | Kept in a box | *Must be accepted as payment | Very old and valuable
exam: «There are legal ways to learn security: puzzle games, competitions and courses.» In this sentence, legal means what? | Loud and noisy | Hidden under the ground | Very old and valuable | *Allowed by the rules and the law
